      "writtenOn": "2018-06-20T18:57:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have had problems relying on this indicator for emergency status in the past. My understanding is that this can return false even in the case that emergency calls are possible because the modem will not do a full scan until we place the request to do the emergency SMS. This will also not work for a phone without a SIM.\n\nFor emergency calling, we will only check to make sure that the modem is on before trying to send the emergency SMS.\n\nAlso, what happens if we are in APM?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 244,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 244,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "3a483e54b834b46d143a74fbb1585e74b6be53dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9768686_be0cc6e7",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ImsSmsDispatcher.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 244,
      "author": {
        "id": 1254163
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-20T22:12:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "QCRIL recently fixed the bug to send emergecny voice registration state(Ex: NOT_REG_MT_SEARCHING_OP_EM). So it should return true for gsm in emergency case.\nFor cdma, I have the fix here https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/707379.\n\nAnd this feature is to send emergency SMS only in LTE or limited LTE so we met modem check condition here.\n\nAnd also Verizon has no requirement of sending this 911 SMS over IMS without SIM.\n\nWe can enhance this feature later when we get more requirements from different operators",
      "parentUuid": "79e33621_ed48a36e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 244,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 244,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "3a483e54b834b46d143a74fbb1585e74b6be53dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
